WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.490
Karen Strode was born sometime in the early
1980s.

00:00:02.490 --> 00:00:06.360
This is evident based on the fact that in
2018, Karen appears to be in her late 30s

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:09.429
or early 40s, and this is further backed up
by the fact that she has a teenage daughter

00:00:09.429 --> 00:00:11.420
who was born in 2000 or 2001.

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.150
It is unclear who Karen’s father could have
been, but Karen is the daughter of Laurie

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.150
Strode.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.740
…Not that daughter.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:21.689
That’s Jamie Lloyd, Laurie’s daughter
in a different timeline.

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:23.070
Think of it as an alternate reality.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:26.019
There’s also a timeline where Laurie has
a son instead of a daughter.

00:00:26.019 --> 00:00:27.910
But in this timeline, it’s just Karen.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:30.009
But Karen and Jamie do share similarities.

00:00:30.009 --> 00:00:33.120
Much like Jamie, she would eventually succumb
to the attacks of Michael Myers, despite her

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.039
mother’s excessive efforts to protect her.

00:00:35.039 --> 00:00:38.870
To learn more about Karen, how Laurie’s
trauma was passed down to her, how she’s

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:42.199
covertly connected to Jamie Lloyd, and why
the writers changed her character to avoid

00:00:42.199 --> 00:00:45.084
controversy, stick around to the end of this
video.

00:00:45.084 --> 00:00:50.248
(metal music)

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:52.620
Welcome to Horror History.

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.200
In today’s lesson, we are taking a deeper
look at the intergenerational trauma passed

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.579
down through the Strode family.

00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:01.320
If you’ve seen other Horror History episodes
on characters from the Halloween franchise,

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.170
then you’re likely familiar with the Halloween
Express, a train map I came up with as an

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.000
analogy to explain the timeline.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.729
Each route is an alternate timeline, and each
stop is a different Halloween movie.

00:01:10.729 --> 00:01:14.270
Karen appears in the 40 Year Timeline, which
follows the original Halloween with Halloween

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:18.590
(2018), Halloween Kills, and then continues
on without Karen in Halloween Ends.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:22.509
For her first appearance in Halloween (2018),
writers were initially planning to name her

00:01:22.509 --> 00:01:25.030
Jamie, as a tribute to her counterpart from
the original timeline.

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:29.189
In a way this makes sense, because both timelines
start with the same Laurie Strode.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:32.910
So if Laurie liked that name in the original
timeline, then I don’t see any reason she

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:34.310
wouldn’t like it in this one.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.729
Jamie and Karen would have been born around
the same time in their respective continuities,

00:01:37.729 --> 00:01:40.790
only a couple years after the timeline split
in 1978.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:44.920
However, they probably didn’t want to confuse
casual audiences into thinking that this was

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:47.050
Jamie, so the name was changed.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.050
To..

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:49.050
Shanah Nelson?

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:50.060
And then, to Karen Nelson.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.900
This was before the Karen meme took off, otherwise,
I’m sure they would have gone with Shanah.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:55.020
Or something else.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:58.020
Actually, if they called her Shanah, then
when they showed her old gun at the end of

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:01.560
Halloween (2018), the initials would have
been SS, and it would have looked like some

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:02.560
Nazi thing.

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:04.689
Maybe it’s best that they just switched
it to Karen.

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:08.360
Karen was raised in what can only be described
as “army boot-camp” like conditions.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.440
Laurie kept her daughter in a very sheltered
and strict home life and started giving her

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.920
some version of combat training, starting
when Karen was only eight years old.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.940
– I learned how to shoot a gun when I was
eight.

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.310
I learned how to fight.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:21.360
I had nightmares about the basement.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:25.060
– To better understand why Laurie put her own
daughter through this instead of doing normal

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.100
80s kid stuff like riding bikes, and…

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.390
I don’t know, basically just riding bikes,
and riding bikes.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:31.770
OH DID I MENTION RIDING BIKES?

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:36.421
…we’re going to have to take it back to
that infamous Halloween night in 1978.

00:02:36.421 --> 00:02:40.941
(haunting music)

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:46.661
In the original 1978 Halloween, Laurie started
out as a relatively happy and normal teenage girl.

00:02:46.661 --> 00:02:49.670
She was considered a good student, she would
talk about crushes with her friends and stow

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:53.090
away her babysitting money, which probably
came in handy when she popped one out before

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.170
finishing college.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:57.840
But on Halloween night in 1978, when all of
Laurie’s friends are murdered by a man in

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:01.200
a William Shatner mask, she is left completely
traumatized.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:04.450
So much so that when some guy in a trenchcoat
who she's never seen before shows up with

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.760
a gun, she doesn’t even question it.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.231
– Was the boogeyman?

00:03:08.231 --> 00:03:12.090
– [Zac] The murder of her friends and subsequent attempt
on her own life, understandably, change Laurie

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.090
forever.

00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:16.540
At some point in her adulthood, she buys a
house on a plot of land at the edge of Haddonfield,

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.390
almost completely isolated from others.

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:21.220
She turns it into her own private bunker and
trap for Michael Myers.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.250
For most of Karen’s childhood, this is where
she was raised.

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.960
– [Ray] What’s this?

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:28.240
–  [Karen] It’s my childhood.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.360
– Laurie is suffering from Post Traumatic Stress
Disorder.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:34.220
It’s not uncommon for parents suffering
from PTSD to pass down what is referred to

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:35.700
as intergenerational trauma.

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:39.830
According to a study by Psychiatric Times:
patients with parents suffering with PTSD

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:43.870
often describe damaged, preoccupied parents
who are emotionally limited.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:48.370
Symptoms in parents such as traumatic reliving,
emotional numbing and dissociative phenomena

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:52.620
do not help a child develop a reasonable sense
of safety and predictability in the world.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:56.560
This would absolutely apply to Karen, as Laurie’s
trauma from the attack left her unable to

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:59.040
be emotionally available for Karen as a parent.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:02.340
Even the interactions they share as adults,
give a pretty clear indication of how Laurie

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:03.840
would have interacted with her as a child:

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:06.290
– [Laurie] You have no security system, Karen.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:09.080
Your side window was wide open.

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:12.650
Sometimes I can’t tell the difference between
your stupidity and your ignorance.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:15.620
– As stated in the intro, it is unclear who
Karen’s father was.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:19.200
When Laurie is interviewed by a pair of investigative
journalists, she mentions that she went through

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:23.270
two divorces but never specifies if either
of her ex-husbands were Karen’s Dad.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:24.750
My guess is: no.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.690
When we see Karen’s old gun, it’s engraved
with the letters KS.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:31.160
She has never been shown to be a Kansas fan,
so the assumption is that this stands for

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:32.160
Karen Strode.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:35.450
If she has her mother’s last name, she was
probably born out of wedlock.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:38.440
Sure, maybe the father’s last name also
started with ‘S’.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:39.440
We don’t know.

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.820
Karen never mentions ever having any kind
of father figure.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:45.680
The only men that we know were in Laurie’s
life at the time are Frank Hawkins, who stated

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:49.840
that he never made it past first base with
Laurie and Ben Tramer, who liked Laurie, but

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:51.690
Laurie still has a crush on him when she’s old enough

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:54.540
to go to a bar, so I’m guessing he’s not
the absent father.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:58.220
– [Hawkins] …But I knew you were sweet for Ben Tramer.

00:04:58.220 --> 00:05:02.380
– [Zac] Either way, Karen was raised by a single mother,
which is already not a good thing, and that

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:06.870
single mother was suffering from PTSD, meaning that
Karen was not afforded with any kind of stability

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:09.840
and had to cope with the effects of her mother’s
trauma alone.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.590
While Laurie may have thought she was protecting
her daughter by teaching her to fight back

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:16.290
against Michael, her actions would have extreme
consequences.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:19.590
When Karen was twelve years old, the Strode
household was visited by social services who

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.340
deemed Laurie unfit to be a mother.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.170
Karen was placed into the foster care system
for the rest of her childhood.

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:26.600
– [Reporter] How long until you regained custody?

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:27.600
– I didn’t.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.810
– In foster care, Karen learned to cope with
the damage that her mother instilled by being

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:34.680
overly optimistic and refusing to see the
world as a “scary” place like Laurie does.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:38.289
There may have been a little bit of an over-correction
on the part of her new caregivers, causing

00:05:38.289 --> 00:05:42.140
her to be a little too trusting of mankind,
but for the most part, it seems they did a

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:46.040
great job with her, because as an adult she
seems integrated as a productive and generally

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:47.950
problem-free member of society.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.740
Karen eventually meets and marries a man named
Ray Nelson.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.840
Ray is the opposite of Laurie in every way.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:56.960
Where Laurie is tough and over-prepared, Ray
is soft and doesn’t overthink things.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.560
In fact, at times, it seems like he hardly
thinks at all.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:04.090
– Daww man! I got peanut butter on my penis.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:08.620
– [Zac] At a very young age, maybe 22 at the oldest,
Karen becomes pregnant with a daughter, and

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:11.960
the addition of the newest member of the family,
has an unintended side effect.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:15.406
Karen’s mother would be coming back into
the picture.

00:06:15.406 --> 00:06:19.506
(impact)

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:24.060
(spooky music)

00:06:24.060 --> 00:06:28.960
Karen and Ray Nelson gave birth to a daughter
in 2000 or 2001 and named her Allyson.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:32.280
Karen tries to raise Allyson completely different
from how Laurie raised her.

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:36.030
Where Laurie showed very little interest in
Karen as a person, Karen goes out of her way

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:38.170
to be actively engaged in Allyson’s life.

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:41.860
She insists on coming to Allyson’s induction
into the National Honor Society, tells her

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:45.210
she’s excited to meet her boyfriend and,
even though Karen avoids celebrating Halloween

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:48.280
due to the fact that the anniversary of the
babysitter murders was the day her mother

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:51.860
was consistently at her craziest, she gives
encouragement when Allyson shares that she’s

00:06:51.860 --> 00:06:53.630
planning on attending the Halloween dance.

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:57.360
Which is pretty significant, since Karen has
grown to hate Halloween so much that she wears

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:59.139
a Christmas sweater on the big day.

00:06:59.139 --> 00:07:02.510
Allyson’s friend at one point suggests
ignoring the holiday altogether, which seems

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:04.050
to be what Karen is going for.

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:05.790
– [Vicky] If I were you guys, I wouldn't celebrate,
either.

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:08.310
I would just put up a Christmas tree instead.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:12.210
– If I lived in Haddonfield, Michael Myers would
be the least of her worries, because she'd

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:13.389
have to answer -- to me.

00:07:13.389 --> 00:07:17.843
But the poor choice of attire is further proof
of Karen’s refusal to follow in Laurie’s footsteps.

00:07:17.843 --> 00:07:21.800
Laurie tried to cope with Halloween by preparing
to fight, Karen copes by finding something

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:22.800
that comforts her.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:26.080
At this point, there are already parallels
we can draw between Karen and Jamie.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:29.820
Jamie also didn’t have much interest in
celebrating, or dressing up for Halloween,

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:33.160
at least at first, she eventually changes
her mind so she can try to fit in with her

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.160
classmates.

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:38.030
In Halloween (2018) we see Laurie trying to
prepare young Karen for an encounter with

00:07:38.030 --> 00:07:40.530
Michael Myers, which she says gives her nightmares.

00:07:40.530 --> 00:07:44.210
In Halloween 4: The Return of Michael Myers,
we also see Jamie having nightmares about

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:47.820
The Boogeyman, implying that at the very least,
Laurie did teach her about her family’s

00:07:47.820 --> 00:07:49.199
history with evil.

00:07:49.199 --> 00:07:52.640
Despite Karen’s best efforts, Laurie’s
trauma still trickles down to Allyson.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:56.490
Allyson feels hurt by Karen’s always active
attempts to keep Laurie away and keeps prodding

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:59.880
to find out if her Mom has invited Laurie
to her Honors celebration dinner.

00:07:59.880 --> 00:08:02.850
Karen lies to her, and states that she did
ask, but that Laurie would not be able to

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:03.850
make it.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:06.850
Allyson is particularly hurt because she knows
her mother is lying.

00:08:06.850 --> 00:08:10.120
But Karen sees this as a way of protecting
her, and we soon see why.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:12.980
Allyson goes around Karen and invites her
Grandmother anyway.

00:08:12.980 --> 00:08:15.070
When Laurie arrives, Karen’s lie is revealed.

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:18.900
However, the issue is immediately put to rest
by Laurie’s own erratic behavior.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:22.020
She shows up drinking and ranting in a way
that makes her look insane.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:26.150
Karen responds by setting boundaries and offering
suggestions, such as “going for a walk”

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:29.560
or “hitting the reset button and starting
over” that seem like something one might

00:08:29.560 --> 00:08:32.539
learn in therapy or even implement as a therapist.

00:08:35.317 --> 00:08:37.590
– [Laurie] I saw him. The Shape.

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:38.595
– Mom...

00:08:38.595 --> 00:08:39.498
– I didn't know what to do.

00:08:39.498 --> 00:08:41.710
– I think maybe this is a little bit too much
for you, huh?

00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:43.330
Why don’t we go for a walk, alright?

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:46.230
You said you were going to try to put the
past behind you.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:47.230
Okay?

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:48.380
Are you going to try to do that?

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:50.029
That’s what you said you wanted to do.

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:50.701
– [Laurie] I can’t.

00:08:50.701 --> 00:08:51.670
– Mom, look at me.

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:54.560
– There is a specific reason that Karen communicates
this way.

00:08:54.560 --> 00:08:58.490
In addition to the therapy that we can safely
assume Karen has gone through, Karen may actually

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:02.430
be a therapist herself, based on the way she
tells Allyson that she “rescheduled her

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:06.010
last session” so that she can attend Allyson’s
induction into the National Honor Society.

00:09:06.010 --> 00:09:10.970
I mean, she could be a personal trainer, or
a prostitute I guess, but she just doesn’t

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:11.970
look the part.

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:15.339
In the original script, she’s actually described
as a “children’s psychologist”; it’s

00:09:15.339 --> 00:09:17.700
not canon in the movie, but I’m kind of
willing to go with that.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.980
It makes sense that Karen would be inspired
to choose a profession where she could help

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:23.040
kids that were going through what she went
though.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:27.110
However, despite Karen making it very clear
how bad her childhood was, and obviously choosing

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:30.960
not to pursue a relationship with her Mom,
Laurie does not regret how she chose to raise

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:31.460
Karen.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:35.310
She still feels it necessary to do what she
considers protecting her by breaking into

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:37.650
her house to point out the lacking security
system.

00:09:37.650 --> 00:09:41.650
It reminds me of those guys on cop shows who
get caught stealing a car, and try to say

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:45.100
they were in the process of returning it…
but like if they were actually telling the

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:45.632
truth.

00:09:45.632 --> 00:09:47.860
– I was just gonna take the car to the police
station.

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:51.540
– Once again, Karen uses the tools she has learned
through therapy to navigate this unwanted

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:55.350
interaction with her Mom, stating that Laurie
“needs to get help” and that she is “not

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:57.090
welcome in this house until she gets it.”

00:09:57.090 --> 00:10:00.490
Also, Ray makes a feeble and embarrassing
attempt to defend Karen.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:04.800
– Hey Laurie, this is my home and I can take care
of my own family, all right?

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:05.800
I know jutjitsu-

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:07.230
– [Zac] Ray thinks he’s Busta Rhymes out here.

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:10.190
Can’t blame Laurie for not trusting Ray
with anyone’s safety.

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:13.180
I can understand Karen’s desire to start
a family that’s going to be different from

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:15.649
her situation growing up, but really?

00:10:15.649 --> 00:10:16.649
This guy?

00:10:16.649 --> 00:10:20.071
It comes as no surprise that Ray is not able
to get Laurie to leave and it’s Karen who

00:10:20.071 --> 00:10:23.770
has to intervene, insisting that the world
is not a “dark and evil place.”

00:10:23.770 --> 00:10:25.100
It’s 2018, Karen.

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.170
If only you stuck around a couple more years.

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:31.320
Unfortunately for Karen, all of Laurie’s
fears were about to come true and no amount

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:34.890
of positive thinking or Christmas sweaters
would be able to prevent the force that is

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:36.260
Michael Myers.

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:39.480
As news of his escape spreads through Haddonfield,
Laurie and Deputy Hawkins are the first to

00:10:39.480 --> 00:10:41.350
take it seriously and spring into action.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:44.790
Hawkins agrees that Michael is likely after
Laurie and her family and assists her in convincing

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.690
Karen to take shelter at Laurie’s house.

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:50.430
However, Allyson is not with Karen, and they
can’t reach her phone, making it impossible

00:10:50.430 --> 00:10:52.420
to track down Allyson’s current whereabouts.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:55.490
Left with little choice, Karen and Ray leave
for Laurie’s house, leaving messages for

00:10:55.490 --> 00:10:56.890
Allyson to meet them there.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:11:00.840
When they arrive, Karen is faced with reminders
of all the past trauma she had tried so hard

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:01.840
to leave behind.

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:05.870
The trap they prepare for Michael in the basement
brings up twisted memories of Karen’s nightmarish

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:08.180
experiences working down there as a girl.

00:11:08.180 --> 00:11:11.350
Despite her feelings about how her childhood
transpired, it’s clear that her training

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:13.050
made her an expert on using a gun.

00:11:13.050 --> 00:11:15.610
– [Laurie] You never wanted to listen to
me when I spoke of that night.

00:11:15.610 --> 00:11:16.610
And this is why.

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.240
I’ve been preparing for this for a long
time.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:21.850
– It doesn’t take long for Michael to find
them, and I’m sure no one will be shocked

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:24.430
to know that Ray is the first to be killed.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:25.430
(Ray screams)

00:11:25.430 --> 00:11:28.520
Karen hides in the basement alone when Michael
breaks in, and she hears her mother’s battle

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.230
with the boogeyman rage on all throughout
the house above her.

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:34.720
It’s during this struggle, that Allyson,
after having her own traumatic night, finds

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:35.790
her way in as well.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.440
Karen calls her downstairs and they both hide
in the basement.

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:41.810
But Michael is able to find the secret entrance,
and muscle the kitchen island that’s blocking

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:42.850
it out of the way.

00:11:42.850 --> 00:11:46.440
With nothing standing between her and her
family’s worst nightmare, Karen begs and

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:50.709
pleads for Laurie to find them, crying that
she can’t do it by herself, and Michael,

00:11:50.709 --> 00:11:53.180
realizing he has a trapped victim, appears
in the stairway.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:54.860
But Karen is only acting.

00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.570
– Gotcha.

00:11:57.797 --> 00:12:01.390
– Despite her attempts to put her childhood
combat training behind her, it is still engrained

00:12:01.390 --> 00:12:03.670
in her memory, like remembering how to ride
a bike.

00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:07.520
Or I guess in her case *instead* of learning
how to ride a bike, because she’s the one

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:09.200
80s kid that didn’t do that.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:13.090
Seeing the horror from Haddonfield first hand
causes Karen to completely drop her “world

00:12:13.090 --> 00:12:16.360
is not a dark and evil place” attitude,
and from that point forward, she becomes just

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.580
as vicious as her mother.

00:12:17.580 --> 00:12:21.300
Allyson and Karen just barely escape Michael’s
grasp as they rush up the stairs and it’s

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:25.190
Karen who activates the bars that lock Michael
into the basement tomb, which is now filling

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.300
up with gas.

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:28.740
Laurie throws in a flare which starts a huge
fire.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:32.440
The entire house has been designed as a trap,
so that if this day ever should come, Michael

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:33.740
would burn down with it.

00:12:33.740 --> 00:12:37.560
We see a doll house in Karen’s old room
go up in flames, which represents Karen’s

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:38.560
childhood.

00:12:38.560 --> 00:12:41.920
Karen always wanted to be a normal kid, but
Laurie wanted to train her for combat.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:45.640
The image represents the trade-off Karen was
forced to make all those years ago -- she’s

00:12:45.640 --> 00:12:48.700
giving up her normal childhood in exchange
for safety as an adult.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:52.089
The three generations of women are able to
flee the house and flag down a ride from a

00:12:52.089 --> 00:12:55.580
couple of Illinois boys, thinking that they
have successfully killed Michael Myers and

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:58.740
ended the terror that has hung over their
town for the last 40 years.

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:01.837
However, this hope would soon be extinguished.

00:13:01.837 --> 00:13:05.081
(impact)

00:13:06.904 --> 00:13:10.810
(spooky music)

00:13:10.959 --> 00:13:14.610
When Laurie, Allyson and Karen, get to the
hospital, Laurie is rushed into emergency

00:13:14.610 --> 00:13:17.290
surgery, leaving Karen and Allyson to cope
with the loss of Ray.

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:21.080
Karen looks at her blood soaked hands and
tries to wash the gory stains from her wedding

00:13:21.080 --> 00:13:24.630
ring, signifying that she’ll never be able
to return to the optimistic life and worldview

00:13:24.630 --> 00:13:27.060
that she had worked so hard to build with
her husband.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:31.495
As Karen and Allyson are questioned by police,
they both learn that Michael survived and escaped.

00:13:31.495 --> 00:13:35.210
Allyson wants to join her boyfriend and the
town mob to go look for Michael and kill him,

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:38.160
while Karen is certain that he will be coming
to the hospital, and that they should stick

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:39.779
close to Laurie and protect her.

00:13:39.779 --> 00:13:43.360
She later goes into her Mom’s room as she’s
waking up, and discovers a note left behind

00:13:43.360 --> 00:13:47.120
by Allyson, explaining that she’s joined
the anti Michael mob, and that it is her love

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:50.380
for her family that is driving her to hunt
him down, not unlike Laurie.

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:53.130
I can only imagine how crushing that was for
her.

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:57.070
She spent her whole parenthood trying to give
Allyson a better life, only to see her become

00:13:57.070 --> 00:14:01.180
a fighter, just like her Grandmother, when
it’s most critical for them to stick together.

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:04.810
Despite this, she does a really impressive
job of keeping it together in order to prevent

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:06.449
Laurie from finding out that Michael survived.

00:14:06.449 --> 00:14:08.800
– She probably just needed some fresh
air.

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:12.500
– The goal is to keep Laurie in bed, so she
can continue to heal, and this is the second

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:16.339
time Karen has manipulated her emotions to
trick someone; the first being when she acted

00:14:16.339 --> 00:14:19.019
like a helpless victim at the foot of the
basement stairs.

00:14:19.019 --> 00:14:22.530
She leaves her mom alone to get some rest,
at which point she runs into Tommy Doyle,

00:14:22.530 --> 00:14:24.540
and only wants to hear one thing from him.

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:25.769
– Where’s my daughter?

00:14:25.769 --> 00:14:29.570
– But even after finding out, she stays at the
hospital, because she really seems to believe

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:33.790
that Michael is after Laurie, whereas Allyson
believes Michael just wants to kill whatever

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:35.000
is in his path.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:38.810
This divide could be explained by the fact
that Allyson sees that Dr. Sartain was the

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:42.089
one to bring Michael and Laurie together,
and Karen doesn’t know about that.

00:14:42.089 --> 00:14:45.390
She’s been told all her life that Michael
is going to come for them, and from her point

00:14:45.390 --> 00:14:48.170
of view, hiding in the basement, that’s
exactly what happened.

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:51.980
And to be fair, if this were any other Halloween
movie, she would have been right.

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:55.850
She watches as Tommy riles up the mob, and
her reaction, to me, says: “they have no

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:57.160
idea what they’re in for.”

00:14:57.160 --> 00:15:00.570
She does her best to stop Tommy from barging
into Laurie's room and revealing that Michael

00:15:00.570 --> 00:15:03.470
Myers is still alive, but he spills the beans
anyway.

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:07.671
Karen tries to justify her lie by saying it
was for her Mom’s safety, which is honestly fair.

00:15:07.671 --> 00:15:11.020
I think it’s one of the few justified lies,
just because it’s a situation where telling

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:14.839
the truth would more than likely put Laurie
directly in harm's way when she needs to focus

00:15:14.839 --> 00:15:15.839
on healing.

00:15:15.839 --> 00:15:19.650
It seems Karen is always willing to bend the
truth to protect those closest to her, as

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:22.990
we saw when she lied to Allyson about inviting
her Grandmother to dinner.

00:15:22.990 --> 00:15:26.660
She insists that, despite what Laurie may
think, all of her preparation was for nothing,

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:31.350
yet, Laurie still firmly disagrees and hilariously
drugs herself up with painkillers.

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:32.930
– AHHH!!!!!!!

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:35.480
–  What the hell did I just witness?

00:15:35.480 --> 00:15:39.199
– The two basically get into a big fight, which
culminates with this:

00:15:39.199 --> 00:15:41.450
– STOP!

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:43.910
I am not gonna let anything happen to you.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:47.709
– Karen has now unsuccessfully begged both her
daughter and mother to stay with her where

00:15:47.709 --> 00:15:50.860
it’s safe, which is another similarity that
she shares with Jamie Lloyd.

00:15:50.860 --> 00:15:54.670
In Halloween 5, Jamie has a vision of danger
at the Halloween party her friend Tina is

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:58.380
going to, but nobody will take her seriously,
and Tina goes to the party anyway.

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:02.260
It is not too long after this that the angry
mob finds another escaped mental patient named

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:05.040
Mr. Tivoli and they mistake him for Michael
Myers.

00:16:05.040 --> 00:16:08.769
Laurie is the first to realize it’s not
Michael, but she gets injured in the stampede,

00:16:08.769 --> 00:16:12.790
so Karen takes it upon herself to try to protect
the man, but despite her best efforts, she’s

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:14.290
unable to save his life.

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:17.490
Back in the hospital room, Hawkins informs
Laurie and Karen about what I was talking

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:21.220
about earlier: the fact that Doctor Sartain
was the one to bring Michael to Laurie earlier

00:16:21.220 --> 00:16:22.220
that evening.

00:16:22.220 --> 00:16:25.930
This revelation makes Karen realize that if
Michael isn’t targeting Laurie, then her

00:16:25.930 --> 00:16:29.050
daughter is in danger of encountering him
out on the streets of Haddonfield.

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:33.657
She gets Tommy to lend her his car and they
devise a plan to lure Michael out into another trap.

00:16:33.657 --> 00:16:37.181
Thanks to Deputy Hawkins’s story, she deduces
that he’s probably headed back home, which

00:16:37.181 --> 00:16:39.889
is likely where Allyson and the others will
be to try to hunt him.

00:16:41.455 --> 00:16:45.890
–  Did you know that when he was
a little boy, he used to stand in his sister’s

00:16:45.890 --> 00:16:49.020
bedroom and stare out the window?

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.740
… Maybe he wasn’t looking out.

00:16:50.740 --> 00:16:52.959
Maybe he was looking in.

00:16:52.959 --> 00:16:54.290
At his reflection.

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:55.290
At himself.

00:16:55.290 --> 00:16:56.480
– She wastes no time getting there.

00:16:56.480 --> 00:17:00.320
Allyson had been traveling with her boyfriend,
Cameron, and Cameron’s dad Lonnie Elam,

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:03.490
so when she saw Lonnie’s empty car outside
the Myers house, she must have feared for

00:17:03.490 --> 00:17:04.490
the worst.

00:17:04.490 --> 00:17:07.519
She grabbed a pitchfork from the Halloween
decorations on the porch, and lucky for her,

00:17:07.519 --> 00:17:08.589
this was a real pitchfork.

00:17:08.589 --> 00:17:10.059
And it’s ****ing massive.

00:17:10.059 --> 00:17:13.679
She shows up just in the nick of time, as
Michael is about to attack Allyson.

00:17:13.679 --> 00:17:17.630
Karen pulls his mask off, just like Laurie
did when he attacked her all those years ago;

00:17:17.630 --> 00:17:19.009
like mother, like daughter.

00:17:19.009 --> 00:17:22.749
And just like he was four decades earlier,
Michael is transfixed by the mask when it

00:17:22.749 --> 00:17:23.749
is taken from him.

00:17:23.749 --> 00:17:27.309
I imagine that Karen knows this because Laurie
taught her everything she knew about Michael

00:17:27.309 --> 00:17:31.509
Myers, based on her experiences that night,
and made sure that she didn't forget a thing.

00:17:31.509 --> 00:17:35.489
So Karen uses the mask to lure him outside,
drawing his attention away from the injured

00:17:35.489 --> 00:17:36.489
Allyson.

00:17:36.489 --> 00:17:39.119
This scene has got to be the biggest Jamie
Lloyd connection of them all.

00:17:39.119 --> 00:17:41.940
Jamie, like Karen, will do anything to protect
her kid.

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:45.639
In Halloween: The Curse of Michael Myers,
Jamie gives birth to a son and uses a similar

00:17:45.639 --> 00:17:47.809
tactic to protect him from the Boogeyman.

00:17:47.809 --> 00:17:51.470
She hides him in a cabinet and runs away with
a bundle of blankets, thereby tricking Michael

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:55.450
into following her as far away as possible
before she finally succumbs to him, and Michael

00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:57.879
is bamboozled upon finding the empty blankets.

00:17:57.879 --> 00:18:01.500
That’s basically what Karen is doing here,
luring Michael out away from her vulnerable

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:02.500
daughter.

00:18:02.500 --> 00:18:04.649
It’s also an important character development
moment for her.

00:18:04.649 --> 00:18:08.520
All night, she’s tried to protect the innocent
people around her: such as her husband, Mr.

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:12.470
Tivoli, heck, even the town of Haddonfield
itself, but she hadn’t found any success

00:18:12.470 --> 00:18:13.740
in saving anybody.

00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:16.799
With her daughter’s life on the line, she
wasn’t going to settle for being too little

00:18:16.799 --> 00:18:17.950
or too late.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:21.940
Michael gives chase, but instead of sacrificing
herself at the end, like Jamie did, she leads

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:25.309
him into a trap where Tommy Doyle and the
angry mob are waiting.

00:18:25.309 --> 00:18:28.720
The sheer numbers of the mob are able to beat
him down, and before going back to be with

00:18:28.720 --> 00:18:31.730
her daughter, Karen gets one good knife shot
into Michael’s upper back.

00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:35.940
She reunites with Allyson and tries to comfort
her, then as she gets up to give the paramedics

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:40.039
some space, she looks up at Michael’s window,
perhaps remembering Frank Hawkins’s story,

00:18:40.039 --> 00:18:44.220
and she sees a strange vision of the child
Michael Myers in his clown costume staring

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.730
out over Haddonfield.

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:49.289
This moment is another that she shares with
her original timeline counterpart, because

00:18:49.289 --> 00:18:53.519
in Halloween 4: The Return of Michael Myers,
Jamie looks into a mirror and sees child Michael

00:18:53.519 --> 00:18:56.519
staring back at her with the same emotionless
expression.

00:18:56.519 --> 00:19:00.460
This is reflective of Frank’s earlier words,
“Maybe he wasn’t looking out.

00:19:00.460 --> 00:19:01.580
Maybe he was looking in.

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:02.899
At his reflection.

00:19:02.899 --> 00:19:03.929
At himself.”

00:19:03.929 --> 00:19:07.950
Karen heads upstairs to see for herself what
Michael might have been looking at, but instead

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:10.840
of seeing her own reflection, she sees Michael’s.

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:14.591
He appears behind her and this time, with
no support network around to help her, he

00:19:14.591 --> 00:19:18.840
takes the knife and finishes her off, the
very last parallel she shares with Jamie Lloyd,

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:23.251
who was also met with a grisly death at the
hands of Haddonfield’s most feared resident.

00:19:23.251 --> 00:19:26.929
I’ve got more episodes lined up for other
40 Year Timeline characters, so let me know

00:19:26.929 --> 00:19:30.480
who else you’d like to see covered here
on Horror History and remember to subscribe

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:35.380
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring
that deathbell and make sure you select ALL notifications.

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:36.800
Please. Please!

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:38.559
I will see you in the next one.

00:19:38.559 --> 00:19:40.470
Assuming we both survive.

